        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SLD8MAGXRNQxXdCwcKoe-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;p&gt;There are &lt;strong&gt;several main types of z-tests&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;, with the most common being the One-Sample Z-Test and the Two-Sample Z-Test, used for comparing means or proportions.&amp;nbsp;These are further categorized into a Z-Test for one proportion and a Two-Proportion Z-Test depending on whether you are comparing a single proportion or two independent proportions from different groups.&amp;nbsp;Additionally, z-tests can be classified by the direction of the hypothesis test into left-tailed, right-tailed, and two-tailed tests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Types of Z-Tests&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEA_enTH1144TH1145&amp;amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=ccc88b753bb383cd&amp;amp;sxsrf=AE3TifN7ouDhrTL3EicZBdncmRKcCTI8Dg%3A1758524585118&amp;amp;q=One-Sample+Z-Test&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg97DJ5uuPAxVZxjgGHXHTE2sQxccNegQIDxAC&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfBcsIoK1Alq5peGeHG0b83TRSrHR7YfjAglZFNM9ucwrK_hz-zaLY4TT7KZ6bHVSPuUArTgiLx_SXSvZmwzpCY19KGdrWaOtxbHm1-IaVy4hMH-su0uSjM9a3tGhCVo15rXmXp3-C_6AM4YvLglYxj8Aw7np5-10gHWcX5lqcd7deU&amp;amp;csui=3&quot;&gt;**One-Sample Z-Test&lt;/a&gt;:**&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Means:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Compares the mean of a single sample to a known or hypothesized population mean when the population standard deviation is known.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Proportions:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Compares a single sample proportion to a known or hypothesized population proportion.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEA_enTH1144TH1145&amp;amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=ccc88b753bb383cd&amp;amp;sxsrf=AE3TifN7ouDhrTL3EicZBdncmRKcCTI8Dg%3A1758524585118&amp;amp;q=Two-Sample+Z-Test&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg97DJ5uuPAxVZxjgGHXHTE2sQxccNegQIFBAC&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfBcsIoK1Alq5peGeHG0b83TRSrHR7YfjAglZFNM9ucwrK_hz-zaLY4TT7KZ6bHVSPuUArTgiLx_SXSvZmwzpCY19KGdrWaOtxbHm1-IaVy4hMH-su0uSjM9a3tGhCVo15rXmXp3-C_6AM4YvLglYxj8Aw7np5-10gHWcX5lqcd7deU&amp;amp;csui=3&quot;&gt;**Two-Sample Z-Test&lt;/a&gt;:**&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Means:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Compares the means of two independent samples to see if they are likely to come from the same population.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Proportions:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Compares the proportions of two independent samples to determine if there&#39;s a significant difference between them.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Categorization by Hypothesis Type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Z-tests can also be classified by the type of hypothesis they are testing:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEA_enTH1144TH1145&amp;amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=ccc88b753bb383cd&amp;amp;sxsrf=AE3TifN7ouDhrTL3EicZBdncmRKcCTI8Dg%3A1758524585118&amp;amp;q=Two-Tailed+Test&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg97DJ5uuPAxVZxjgGHXHTE2sQxccNegQIMxAB&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfBcsIoK1Alq5peGeHG0b83TRSrHR7YfjAglZFNM9ucwrK_hz-zaLY4TT7KZ6bHVSPuUArTgiLx_SXSvZmwzpCY19KGdrWaOtxbHm1-IaVy4hMH-su0uSjM9a3tGhCVo15rXmXp3-C_6AM4YvLglYxj8Aw7np5-10gHWcX5lqcd7deU&amp;amp;csui=3&quot;&gt;**Two-Tailed Test&lt;/a&gt;:**&amp;nbsp;Tests if there is a difference between two groups or a sample and a population, but doesn&#39;t specify the direction of the difference.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEA_enTH1144TH1145&amp;amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=ccc88b753bb383cd&amp;amp;sxsrf=AE3TifN7ouDhrTL3EicZBdncmRKcCTI8Dg%3A1758524585118&amp;amp;q=Left-Tailed+Test&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg97DJ5uuPAxVZxjgGHXHTE2sQxccNegQINRAB&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfBcsIoK1Alq5peGeHG0b83TRSrHR7YfjAglZFNM9ucwrK_hz-zaLY4TT7KZ6bHVSPuUArTgiLx_SXSvZmwzpCY19KGdrWaOtxbHm1-IaVy4hMH-su0uSjM9a3tGhCVo15rXmXp3-C_6AM4YvLglYxj8Aw7np5-10gHWcX5lqcd7deU&amp;amp;csui=3&quot;&gt;**Left-Tailed Test&lt;/a&gt;:**&amp;nbsp;Tests if the population mean or proportion is less than a specific value or if one group&#39;s mean/proportion is less than another&#39;s.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEA_enTH1144TH1145&amp;amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=ccc88b753bb383cd&amp;amp;sxsrf=AE3TifN7ouDhrTL3EicZBdncmRKcCTI8Dg%3A1758524585118&amp;amp;q=Right-Tailed+Test&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg97DJ5uuPAxVZxjgGHXHTE2sQxccNegQINhAB&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfBcsIoK1Alq5peGeHG0b83TRSrHR7YfjAglZFNM9ucwrK_hz-zaLY4TT7KZ6bHVSPuUArTgiLx_SXSvZmwzpCY19KGdrWaOtxbHm1-IaVy4hMH-su0uSjM9a3tGhCVo15rXmXp3-C_6AM4YvLglYxj8Aw7np5-10gHWcX5lqcd7deU&amp;amp;csui=3&quot;&gt;**Right-Tailed Test&lt;/a&gt;:**&amp;nbsp;Tests if the population mean or proportion is greater than a specific value or if one group&#39;s mean/proportion is greater than another&#39;s.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="660" x="-16393.79" y="8461.87" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
